node_modules
dist
coverage
frontend
.git

# Secrets must never be baked into an image layer — they are passed at runtime
# via env_file / secret mounts, and an image layer survives deleting the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# A `*` does not cross a `/`, so `*.pem` matches only the context root — the TLS
# material under deploy/ needs the `**/` form. The bare patterns are kept as well
# even though `**/` also matches at the root: this is the one exclusion whose
# failure mode is a private key baked into an image layer that survives deleting
# the file, and two redundant lines are a trivial price for not having to be
# right about one matcher's semantics.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
deploy/certbot
deploy/mosquitto

mosquitto/config/passwd
CLAUDE.md
